        "sha256": "450a335ed6563a7f4a5cc380f2bbe72f98b70e532ac2c8d16a679bcc545d4900",
        "lines": 16070,
        "previous": {
          "path": "PIXEL-ART-ASSETS.md",
          "sha256": "450a335ed6563a7f4a5cc380f2bbe72f98b70e532ac2c8d16a679bcc545d4900",
          "lines": 16070
        }
      },
      "retrieved": {
        "text": "FOR INTERACTION INSTANCES LIKE LADDER REPAIRS, LOOTING, SALVAGING, ETC, THERE SHOULD BE A STYLIZED KEYBOARD KEY BUTTON BESIDE THE PLAYER. THE BOTTOM LEFT IS TOO FAR FROM THE CENTRE EYELINE AS THE ONLY OPTION. THEY DO NOT NEED TO BE REMOVED. THEY SHOUDL STAY THERE. BUT A MINIMIAL [E] WITH A DOWN ARROW ONTOP SHOULD BE PROVIDED BESIDE THE CHARACTER AS AN INDICATOR THEY CAN PRESS THAT BUTTON, AS IN, SOMETHING NEAR THEM IS INTERACTABLE; IF THEY WANT TO KNOW EXACTLY WHAT THEY HAVE TO LOOK AT THE BOTTOM LEFT FOR THE FULL TOOLTIP LIKE IT IS RIGHT NOW. BELOW IS A DIRECT EXAMPLE YOU SHOULD USE FOR THE BUTTON. USE THE THIRD ONE THAT HAS THE DEPRECATION(PUSHING DOWN) ANIMATION. IT SHOULD BE ADJUSTED AND RELEVANT SIZE TO THE GAME WITHOUT LOSING CLARITY. ADDITIONALLY, IF THE USER PRESSES E FOR INTERACT, THAT BUTTON SHOULD REACT TO THE USERS INPUT, AS IN PLAY THE ANIMATION FOR THE BUTTON PRESS.\r\n\r\nTHE ABOVE LOGIC CAN BE USED TO OVERHAUL A SIGNIFICANT PORTION OF THE UI, WHILE ADJUSTING IT TO FIT THE UI COLOR SCHEME. ULTIMATELY; THIS IS YOUR DECISION TO BALANCE. DO NOT UNDER SATURATE AND CREATE CLEARLY OUT OF PLACE CONTRASTING ASSETS. DO NOT OVER SATURATE AND DESTROY THE DESIGN BALANCE BY CREATING A OVER CONCENTRATION OF THE PIXEL AESTHETIC IN BUTTONS ONLY AND ONTHING ELSE. ITS ABOUT BALANCE WITH THE PROVIDED ASSETS, TWEAKING AND POLISHING WHAT NEEDS TO BE. CHANGES CAN BE SMALL, BUT NEED TO BE CONSISTENT APPLICATION WIDE. WE DONT CHANGE ONE THING AND CALL IT AESTHETICALLY UPDATED. WE UPDATE IT TO FIT ACROSS THE APPLIATIONS AESTHETICS.\r\n\r\nTHIS STEP IS MORE OF A PIXEL ART UI OVERHAUL BALANCE. INTRODUCTION WHERE NECESSARY, ADJUSTMENTS IN OTHER PLACES TO BALANCE IT. OVERALL COHESIVE CHOICES IN DESIGN, BALANCE AMONGST THE MODERN AND RETRO.\r\n",
        "sha256": "450a335ed6563a7f4a5cc380f2bbe72f98b70e532ac2c8d16a679bcc545d4900",
        "start": 11,
        "end": 15,
        "bytes": 1749
      }
    }
  ],
